Well, I don't really mind that some people are use to using pounds and
ounces =97 except in science and engineering, where it can cause all
sorts of problems.

I've just pushed a update which adds a new config option, called
"weight_system". It can be set in the config file, and it can be
changed while playing. The options are 'metric',
'avoirdupois' (pounds / ounces), 'game', and 'none'. Game units are
just the raw numbers that are used by the game internally; and 'none'
means that weights will not be displayed at all.

While I'm posting, I might as well tell you all about a potential
change for riding that I've been considering. I don't like that
improving riding beyond 'basic' is essentially useless, and I don't
like that falling off while trying to mount is so common - and so
dangerous for young knights.

So I've got some ideas for changes (which I haven't implemented yet).
It would look roughly like this:
unskilled: often fail to mount, can't pickup while riding, ~1/50
chance of walking in a random direction instead of chosen direction.
basic: rarely fail to mount, can pickup, ~1/50 chance of the mount
refusing to move - but will not walk randomly.
skilled: never fail to mount unless fumbling, mount always follows
directions
expert: making the mount gallop does not reduce tameness, can ride
down stairs while burdened

If I implemented these changes, I'd probably also increase the maximum
riding skill of some roles. Ranger, from basic->skilled, Barbarian,
basic->skilled, and maybe even Valkyries skilled->expert... I expect
expert riding would still be very rare anyway.


